nterpret abuse inflicted upon women without the risk of redoubling an injustice they can scarcely understand. Driver stated that she believes that there is no hierarchy of abuse and that women should be allowed to speak up. Driver stated that she believes that men should listen and not have an opinion on how women should be metabolizing abuse. Driver stated that she"}
{"input": "", "answers": ["Microsoft unveiled its much-hyped Project Natal motion control system—now renamed “Kinect”—at E3 last night, in a performance long on grandiosity and short on actual revelations. After walking through a set of fake living rooms, the white-poncho-wearing audience was treated to a performance by Cirque du Soleil acrobats dressed as cavemen, as a narrator declared that “history is about to rewritten” and a boy, raising his arms, used his movements usher in the new motion-based way to play games, according to the Wall Street Journal. And what was this grand historical event all about? Well, mostly mimicking the Wii, according to CNET. Microsoft’s camera-based motion controller may have potential, but the games demoed last night mostly looked like analogues for successful Wii efforts, including a yoga game, a racing game, and a Wii Sports-esque game titled—wait for it—Kinect Sports. IGN has a full list of launch titles. Microsoft is expected to reveal more details, including pricing, at its press conference today."], "length": 2768, "dataset": "multi_news", "pred": "Microsoft has finally given its motion-sensing controller for Xbox 360 a name: Kinect. The company unveiled the new name during a special performance at the University of Southern California's Galen Center in Los Angeles. The performance included Cirque du Soleil acrobats, a 9-foot tall elephant puppet, and audience members wearing white poncho-like shoulder pads. The event was meant to give audience members a sneak peek at Kinect and its pricing details, which will be unveiled at Microsoft's press conference on Monday. Kinect is seen as a competitor to Nintendo's Wii, which popularized motion gaming. Unlike the Wii, Kinect does not require a controller and can recognize a wider range of movements, including voices. Microsoft has announced a number of games that will accompany Kinect, including a Yoga/Tai Chi game, a soccer game, Joyride, Kinect Sports, Kinectimals, Kinect Adventures, Dance Central, and a racing game. The company has also demonstrated dashboard apps that use motion controls to interact with Netflix."}
{"input": "", "answers": ["Get out your checkbooks, kids: There is a slew of famous and infamous items up for auction. The US Marshal's office's online auction of the Unabomber's personal effects ends tomorrow, and Aol's Weird News astutely observes that Ted Kaczynski's 35,000-word handwritten manifesto ($17,525) is currently going for less than the gray hoodie ($20,025) that figured so prominently into his FBI Wanted poster. Bonus: sunglasses included. Looking for more of a bargain? A bow and arrows in a Sears box is currently a steal at $743. And in other bizarre auction news: Balloon boy's dad is trying to auction off the infamous \"flying saucer\" balloon for $1 million. But don't worry, reports KTLA: Richard Heene has vowed to give all the money to charity (specifically, Japan). A bunch of celebrities are hoping JetBlue loses their luggage ... right into the hands of eager bidders. The Celebrity Baggage Auction will benefit DoSomething.org. Buy a signed Jessica Simpson-brand bag or a leather Coach bag personally used by Rosario Dawson, and get two roundtrip JetBlue tickets, too. Click for more. Maybe eBay is the place to buy stuff: Morace Park bought a film reel for $5.25 that turned out to be the only known copy of the Charlie Chaplin film Zepped. The Telegraph reports that it's expected to fetch six figures in a June 29 auction."], "length": 1551, "dataset": "multi_news", "pred": "The Unabomber's personal effects are currently up for auction. The items include his 35,000 word manifesto, his iconic hoodie, and his Smith-Corona typewriter. The auction is raising money to pay off a restitution order to the victims of his mail bombings. The items are expected to fetch a total of $15 million, but so far, only a few items have attracted serious bids. The auction ends on June 2."}
{"input": "", "answers": ["A former Boston TV news anchor says that last year, when her son was 18, he was at a bar in Natucket, Mass., when he met Kevin Spacey. The actor \"bought him drink after drink after drink and when my son was drunk, Spacey made his move and sexually assaulted him,\" said Heather Unruh at a press conference Wednesday. She says Spacey stuck his hand down her son's pants and onto his genitals, and tried to convince him to go to a party where they could continue to drink, USA Today reports. A bystander asked the teen if he was OK and the teen said no, at which point the woman urged the teen to flee and he took her advice, Unruh said. Unruh, who appeared with an attorney, says her son filed a police report last week and handed over evidence; she says a criminal investigation has been opened but the Nantucket Police Department has not confirmed that. The attorney with Unruh noted that her son's accusations are \"well within\" both the civil and criminal statutes of limitations. USA Today has a list of the 14 people so far accusing Spacey of sexual assault or harassment. Meanwhile Jon Bernthal, who worked with Spacey on Baby Driver, told a SiriusXM radio show Tuesday that he lost respect for Spacey while working on the film. \"I thought he was a bit of a bully,\" Bernthal said, per People. \"I didn’t really care for the way he was behaving toward some of the other people on set.\""], "length": 3331, "dataset": "multi_news", "pred": "Kevin Spacey has been accused by more than a dozen men of sexual harassment, assault, or attempted rape in allegations spanning decades since Oct. 29. The latest developments include: Spacey to be cut entirely from 'All the Money in the World' Netflix officially parts ways with Spacey Former TV news anchor Heather Unruh says Spacey assaulted her son in a bar in Massachusetts in 2016 Spacey's representatives did not immediately respond to requests for comment."}
{"input": "", "answers": ["Since we last checked in, the situation in Mali following a soldiers' coup has spiraled, with rising concerns over food and gas shortages, violence, and indeed the country's \"very existence,\" according to Le Monde. An update: The coup has driven more than 200,000 people from their homes to other parts of the region, the AP reports. The UN worries that major food shortages could be imminent, and \"mayhem in these towns and cities is increasing,\" says a rep. Neighboring countries have established an embargo against the rebels who ousted the president; they've closed off their borders and frozen the country's regional bank account. That has prompted residents of Mali, which imports all its fuel, to rush to gas stations to collect fuel. The country's electricity grid may also be headed for failure. UNESCO is citing a threat to Timbuktu, a World Heritage Site full of \"architectural wonders,\" notes the BBC. Mosques there are \"essential to the preservation of the identity of the people of Mali,\" says the group. Yet \"nothing seems to be able to stop\" the Tuareg coup, Le Monde reports. West African leaders need to help Mali's military fight back before the instability spreads beyond the country's borders."], "length": 2503, "dataset": "multi_news", "pred": "The north of Mali is currently in the hands of a Tuareg rebellion. The rebels, who are mostly members of the nomadic Tuareg people, want to establish an independent state called Azawad. The rebels currently only hold the northern part of Mali, but with potential reinforcements from neighboring countries, they could soon control the entire country. The Malian army is falling apart, and the junta that overthrew the president has not sent any troops to defend the country from the rebels. The West African leaders are trying to prevent the collapse of the Malian state and have formed a diplomatic committee to threaten the junta with sanctions if they do not relinquish power. The rebels have 